Fusion VTT - third-party notices
================================

This file collects attributions for third-party material that Fusion VTT uses or
produces (spec 26, REQ-LEG-023). The release pipeline (`pnpm build:release`) copies
it next to the executable and into the avatar acervo folder. Sections for other
third-party material are added here as they are inventoried.


Avatar art (Liberated Pixel Cup)
--------------------------------

The avatar creator draws characters from the `waybuilder-avatar` acervo, built from
the Liberated Pixel Cup (LPC) "Universal LPC Spritesheet Character Generator":

  https://github.com/LiberatedPixelCup/Universal-LPC-Spritesheet-Character-Generator

Each piece has its own license (CC-BY-SA 3.0, CC-BY 3.0/4.0, OGA-BY 3.0, CC0, ...)
and its own authors; 69 authors are credited. The full list, with the license of
every piece, is the acervo's `creditos.json` (shown in the avatar creator, REQ-AVT-019,
and shipped as `avatar/creditos.json` with `avatar/LICENSES.txt`).

Art from this acervo is NOT embedded in the Fusion executable. It is distributed as
the optional folder `avatar/`, installed next to the executable (see
`avatar/LICENSES.txt`).

PNG images generated by the avatar creator ("Usar como token" / "Usar como retrato")
are treated as derivative works under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (the most restrictive non-GPL
license among the pieces), with attribution to the Liberated Pixel Cup authors. The
attribution is written inside every generated PNG as `tEXt` chunks (`Source`,
`License`, `Credits-URL`, `Credits`). Anyone who redistributes such an image must keep
it and license the derivative work under the same terms.

This is a project decision, not legal advice (provisional, 2026-10-21; see
specs/35-avatar-do-personagem.md section 6.1).


